============================================================
STAGE-WISE STRUCTURE
============================================================

Display the topic as meaningful learning stages.

Example ONLY:

Stage 1
Programming Foundations

Stage 2
Variables & Data

Stage 3
Control Flow

Stage 4
Functions

Stage 5
Data Structures

Stage 6
Practical Python

Stage 7
Mastery

IMPORTANT:

Do NOT hardcode these stages into the product.

They are an example of the visual structure.

The system must render whatever learning stages exist in the generated TopicCurriculumPlan.

Each stage should show:

- stage number
- title
- short objective
- concepts covered
- prerequisite indication

Keep each card concise.

============================================================
LEARNING GRAPH
============================================================

The result screen MUST include a learning graph/map.

This is NOT a developer architecture diagram.

It is the learner's map.

It should answer:

"What do I need to learn to reach my goal?"

Show relationships such as:

TARGET TOPIC
      │
      ▼
  Stage 1
      │
      ▼
  Stage 2
    ↙   ↘
 Concept A  Concept B
      │
      ▼
  Stage 3
      │
      ▼
   MASTERY

The graph should display:
- current/available stages
- prerequisites
- dependencies
- final target

Do not make it overly complicated.

